_USECASE_TEST_BRIEF = """\
You are a TESTING-DEV session running use case {uc_id} for project '{slug}'.
Your job is to walk this user flow MANUALLY (playwright MCP) on the real app,
capture evidence per step, and report a pass/fail verdict — NOT to change code.

== USE CASE: {title} ({uc_id}) ==
- Persona:          {persona}
- Goal:             {goal}
- Preconditions:    {preconditions}
- Success criteria: {success_criteria}
- Related tickets:  {related}

Steps to walk:
{steps}{feedback_block}

== HOW TO TEST (manual-first, T-0158) ==
1. SCENARIO NARRATION. Restate the flow in your own words first; confirm the
   preconditions hold (auth, data, target env = staging.botsquad.dev). If a
   precondition can't be met, STOP and report it as a blocker.
2. EVIDENCE PER STEP. Drive each step with the playwright MCP. After each step,
   take a screenshot and note expected-vs-actual. Do not batch — one observation
   per step, so a failure is pinned to the exact step.
3. PASS/FAIL RUBRIC. The run PASSES only if every step's actual matches expected
   AND the success criterion is observably met. Any deviation = FAIL.
4. REGRESSION-VS-NEW-ISSUE TRIAGE. For each failure decide: is this a REGRESSION
   (worked before / contradicts a related-ticket DoD) or a NEW ISSUE (gap never
   covered)? Label it. Cross-check the prior feedback above — a failure that
   matches old feedback is a regression of a known fix.
5. RECORD. Write the walkthrough + evidence into a scenario file
   (`bsq scenario new` style) under data/{slug}/scenarios/ or note results on the
   related tickets. File a backlog ticket via `task_new` for every confirmed
   issue (never hand-pick a T-id). Submit process friction with
   `bsq feedback submit --usecase {uc_id} '<note>'`.
6. REPORT. When done, peer-send a one-line PASS/FAIL summary to {report_to}
   (`bsq peer send {report_to} 'UC {uc_id}: PASS|FAIL — <n> issues, <m> regressions'`).

FIRST read AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md for paths + the staging JWT/playwright recipe.
Track all work on tickets, never in superpowers docs. Run `bsq --help` for verbs.
"""


